  "statement": {
    "title": "Triton can elide the y-mask when y-grid wrapping still needs it",
    "body": "TritonKernel._has_constant_mask treats a block-aligned dimension as mask-free. For a Y dimension whose logical size exceeds the hardware y-grid limit, grid wrapping can still create out-of-range lanes unless a Z dimension already handles the overflow. Keep the existing optimization for X, bounded Y, and explicit Z, but conservatively retain the Y mask when the logical Y size can overflow the grid.",
